            <ArticleTitle>Torsion of the fallopian tube and acute pelvic pain: an unusual presentation of genital tuberculosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1810-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.fertnstert.2007.09.063</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of a genital tuberculosis found during laparoscopic evaluation for recurrent acute pelvic pain is presented. The symptoms of genital tuberculosis can vary greatly, and a laparoscopic approach is effective for making the diagnosis. Clinicians should consider tuberculosis as a differential diagnosis when encountering clinical presentations of pelvic pain and ascites.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
